# Standalone Mode

Applies for bug fixes, GitHub issues, one-off tasks, and any work without docs/feat/wip infrastructure.

## Entry Procedure

After the basic instructions in SKILL.md load, collect request/target metadata only. Do not investigate issue bodies or source, trace behavior or reproduce the bug here; the common execution phase owns requirement and source investigation after profile loading.

1. Identify the requested scope and any issue reference from the user's prompt.
2. Collect candidate target filenames from the request, file listings and diff metadata. This initial set drives profile detection; when the request supplies no paths, use a conservative candidate list from the affected directories. The common investigation phase may refine it and load additional guidance.

**Knowledge sources for the common investigation phase:** `kk:arch-decisions`, `kk:project-conventions`, `kk:lang-idioms`, `kk:review-findings`, and `kk:debug-context`. That phase establishes explicit outcomes, constraints and consequential ambiguities from the request, referenced issue and repository instructions. Keep inferred intent provisional; do not invent product requirements or require a full feature plan.

After completing the entry procedure, return to SKILL.md Step 2 (Execute).

Keep change context conversational and proportionate. Trivial fixes skip only the approach statement, never instruction/profile loading or applicable dependency handling. Material deferred work belongs in existing tracking or a concise repository-local review note with owner (or unassigned), reason, next action and verification condition. Completion uses the same hard-requirement and evidence gates as plan mode.
